            <ArticleTitle>Clinical Pattern of Bullous Disorders in Eastern Libya.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>337-339</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A retrospective clinical analysis of 66 patients with various bullous disorders seen over a period of 5 years in Benghazi, Libya showed that pemphigus vulgaris was the commonest disorder followed by buuous' petaphigoid. Other bullous dermatoses were rare. The clinical picture and treatment schedule with follow up of some patient is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
